  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Zero runs on four hits. That's the game they played yesterday, and it cost them.",
    "what_this_means": "They never trailed by more than one, but trailing is all they did. From the second inning onward, the scoreboard read Seattle 1, Yankees 0. A gap that should have closed a dozen times. They put runners on in the second with three at-bats to work with and left them all standing. The third brought another chance, another empty result. By the time they mounted any real pressure, Fried had already left the building with his lead intact, and the bullpen. Yarbrough, De los Santos, Cruz. Locked the door clean. Ten strikeouts in a game this tight is not a slump. It's a locked door that nobody had the key for. The formula works when the bats finish what the pitching allows. Yesterday they didn't.",
    "what_to_watch": "Shane Bieber takes the mound tonight against Gerrit Cole, who has posted a 2.14 ERA over his last four starts. Cole enters this game needing exactly what the offense could not deliver yesterday: run support against a pitcher vulnerable enough to let it slip through.",
